<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Snowdonia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eryri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Snowdonia, in Welsh Eryri, is a mountainous region of north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> around Snowdon, at 1,085 metres the highest mountain in Wales. Its natural fortress sheltered the princes of Gwynedd, and it was the last area of Wales to fall to Edward I in 1282–1283. Since 1951 it has been a national park.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/snowdonia.jpg" alt="Snowdonia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scott Wylie from UK · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snowdon_Ranger_path_on_a_cold_February_day._(16431627106).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
